<statement>
<p>
A population of bacteria is growing according to the equation <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({t}\right)}={1850}{e}^{{{0.21}{t}}}</m>.  Estimate when the population will exceed 4024.</p>
<p>
<em>t</em>= <fillin characters="20"/>   </p>
<p>
Give your answer accurate to one decimal place.
</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>3.7004323509867</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p><m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({t}\right)}={1850}{e}^{{{0.21}{t}}}</m></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{4024}={1850}{e}^{{{0.21}{t}}}</m></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle\frac{{4024}}{{1850}}={e}^{{{0.21}{t}}}</m></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\ln{{\left(\frac{{4024}}{{1850}}\right)}}}={0.21}{t}</m></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle\frac{{\ln{{\left(\frac{{4024}}{{1850}}\right)}}}}{{0.21}}={t}</m></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{t}={3.7004323509867}</m></p></solution>
</myopenmath>